G54: real shutdown and restart (PSCI CPU_OFF, SYSTEM_OFF, SYSTEM_RESET).

SweetCPU::quiesceCPU() panicked and PE_halt_restart was NULL, so iOS's
"slide to power off" panicked the G54 (owner, E35). quiesceCPU now powers
the CPU down with PSCI CPU_OFF (it returns through CPU_ON), haltCPU waits in
WFI, and PE_halt_restart maps halt to PSCI SYSTEM_OFF and restart to PSCI
SYSTEM_RESET after clearing the MT6855 watchdog reboot-mode nibble
(TOPRGU 0x1c007000 + 0x24) that the g54-xnu loader sets to Fastboot, so a
user restart boots normally. Panic paths are unchanged.

Multi-instruction inline asm separates instructions with "\n\t", never ";":
Apple's arm64 assembler treats ";" as a comment, so "dsb sy; smc #0"
silently dropped the smc (K11, g54-xnu E38: SYSTEM_OFF returned and the
0209 halt timer panicked).

